  "slug": "ageing-germ-layer-5e5f",
  "summary": "Five preprints advance isogenic, immortalised and pluripotent-derived models of vascular, cardiac and myogenic lineages, with benchmarking of developmental fidelity.",
  "synthesis": "The current items share a focus on building and benchmarking cell models of defined lineages, in cardiovascular and muscle systems. Isogenic hiPSC-derived vascular smooth muscle cells compare monosomy-X with euploid lines and reveal donor-specific transcriptomic effects. A single-cell atlas integrating 16 heart organoid datasets benchmarks developmental fidelity across protocols, while a second heart field route yields right ventricular, atrial and left ventricular cardiomyocytes. Two items extend proliferative capacity without transgene integration: CDKN2A knockout by mRNA delivery immortalises non-tumorigenic bovine satellite cells that retain myogenic differentiation, and transient hTERT mRNA adds 2-6 population doublings in Duchenne myogenic progenitors. The new element is the pairing of genetic or protocol control with explicit fidelity or donor-effect readouts. All five are preprints.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
